---
title: "2 · Edit lines, adjustments and GST"
description: Use the invoice editor - the left panel, the line items from the service catalog, tax codes, service periods, discounts and fees, tax-inclusive amounts, GST and the printed sections.
sidebar:
  order: 3
  label: "2 · Edit lines, adjustments and GST"
---

**Who:** any member who can see the client or the opportunity. **Where:** the invoice editor, which opens when an invoice is created, or from **Edit invoice** on the invoice page.

The editor has a panel on the left and the invoice paper on the right. You edit directly on the paper; what you see is what the client will receive.

## The top bar

| Button | What it does |
|---|---|
| **Save draft** / **Save changes** | Saves the invoice. It reads **Save draft** until the first save and **Save changes** after it. It is greyed out when there is nothing to save. |
| **Issue** | Issues the draft. See [Issue and send](/en/invoices/issue-send/). |
| **Preview** / **Edit** | Shows the paper as it will be printed, without the left panel, and switches back. |
| **More actions** › **Download as PDF** | Downloads the saved invoice as a PDF. Save your changes first. |
| **Close** | Leaves the editor. With unsaved changes, Operon asks first: **Keep editing** or **Exit without saving**. |

## The left panel

The panel has two tabs. Select **Collapse panel** to give the paper more room.

**Association** shows what the invoice belongs to:

- **Recipient**: the client the invoice is addressed to. The **To** rows on the paper are filled from this client's record. **Change recipient** opens a client search. It is offered while the invoice's amounts can still be edited: on a draft, or on an issued invoice with no payment and no credit applied. Once a payment or credit is recorded, it is no longer offered.
- **Opportunity** and **Contract**: shown for information. An invoice from a contract stays linked to it.
- **Reference**: the client's purchase order number or their own reference, for example `PO-7781`. Optional, up to 100 characters. See [The customer reference](#the-customer-reference).
- **Issuing entity**: the company that issues the invoice. Its GST settings, bank account and number series apply. After the invoice is issued, the issuing entity can no longer be changed.

**Settings** holds **Amounts are** (**Tax exclusive** or **Tax inclusive**; see [Tax-inclusive amounts](#tax-inclusive-amounts)) and the layout of this invoice: the **Serial number format** (read-only here), **Locale**, **Currency** (only SGD in this release), **Date format**, **Default due date**, **Theme colour** and the **Invoice sections**. The sections are switched on or off one by one:

| Section | Prints |
|---|---|
| **Logo image** | The logo at the top. |
| **Due date** | The due date. |
| **Description** | A free-text description. |
| **Payment details** | The issuing entity's bank account and PayNow UEN. |
| **Signature image** | An uploaded signature image. |
| **Signature collection** | A block for the client to sign, with **Include counter signature** for a second signer. |
| **Footer note** | A note at the bottom, with an optional **Border**. |

Changes made here apply to this invoice only. The template itself is not changed.

## Line items

{% steps %}

1. Select **New Item** under the table. An empty line is added.
2. In the name cell, type part of a service name and pick the service from the list. Only services in the service catalog can be used; a name that matches no service cannot be saved.
3. Enter the **Quantity** and check the **Price**. The price comes from the catalog and can be changed for this invoice.
4. To give a discount or a fee on one line, select the line's **Adjustment** cell, choose **Discount** or **Fee**, choose **Percentage** or **Fixed amount**, and enter the value.
5. To change the order, drag a line by its handle. To remove a line, select **Delete line**.

{% /steps %}

New services are added to the service catalog by the department head, not in the invoice (see [Services & Packages](/en/crm/services-packages/)).

## Columns

Select a column header to open its toolbar: **Move left**, **Move right**, **Add column**, **Column settings** and **Delete column**. **Add column** offers **Text**, **Discount**, **Fee**, **Multiplier** and, when they are not already on the table, **Tax**, **Description**, **SKU**, **Adjustment** and **Service period**. Column names can be edited. **Name**, **Price**, **Quantity** and **Total** are required columns and cannot be deleted.

## Discounts and fees on the whole invoice

{% steps %}

1. Under the subtotal, select **Adjustment**.
2. Choose **Discount · Percentage**, **Discount · Fixed amount**, **Fee · Percentage** or **Fee · Fixed amount**.
3. Enter a label and the value. To remove an adjustment, select **Remove adjustment**.

{% /steps %}

Adjustments are applied in the order listed. Each one is worked out on the amount left by the ones above it, starting from the subtotal. A discount cannot be larger than the amount it applies to.

## GST

GST is calculated by Operon. It cannot be typed in or added as an adjustment.

- When the issuing entity is not registered for GST, no GST is charged and no tax column is printed.
- When it is registered, each line is taxed by its tax code. **SR** (standard-rated) lines are taxed at the issuing entity's GST rate; **ZR** (zero-rated), **ES** (exempt) and **OS** (out of scope) lines are not taxed. A line picked from the catalog takes its tax code from the service.
- Discounts and fees on the whole invoice are shared across the tax codes in proportion to their amounts before GST is worked out.
- A GST-registered issuing entity always prints **Tax Invoice** as the title.

### The tax code of each line

When the issuing entity is GST-registered, every line has a **Tax code**: **SR**, **ZR**, **ES** or **OS**. Choose it on the line.

- When the layout has a **Tax** column, the code is chosen in that column and printed on the invoice.
- When the layout has no **Tax** column, the editor adds a **Tax code (not printed)** column at the end of the table. The code still decides the line's GST, but the column is shown only in the editor: **Preview**, the invoice page and the PDF do not show it. To print the codes, add a **Tax** column.

When the issuing entity is not GST-registered, no tax code can be chosen and no **Tax** column is printed.

{% screenshot id="invoices/editor-tax-code-not-printed" caption="A layout with no Tax column: the Tax code (not printed) column at the end of the table." /%}

## A worked example

ABC PTE. LTD. is invoiced for two services. The issuing entity is GST-registered at 9%.

| Line or adjustment | Amount (SGD) |
|---|---|
| Monthly retainer, 1 × 1,200.00, line discount 10% | 1,080.00 |
| Annual return filing, 2 × 350.00 | 700.00 |
| **Subtotal** | 1,780.00 |
| Discount, fixed amount | −50.00 |
| Fee 5% (of 1,730.00) | 86.50 |
| GST 9% (of 1,816.50) | 163.49 |
| **Total** | 1,979.99 |

## Service period

A line can carry the period of the service it bills, for example the months of a retainer.

{% steps %}

1. Add a **Service period** column (**Add column** › **Service period**).
2. In the line's cell, enter the **Service period start** and the **Service period end**. To remove the period, select **Clear service period**.

{% /steps %}

The column prints the period as months when it covers whole months, for example `Jan 2026 – Dec 2026`, or `Nov 2026` for a single month. Otherwise it prints the days, for example `15 Mar 2026 – 14 Mar 2027`. A line without a period prints an empty cell.

The start cannot be after the end. Such a line shows **The start date is after the end date.**, and the invoice cannot be saved until the dates are corrected.

When the layout has no **Service period** column but a line carries a period, the editor shows a **Service period (not printed)** column. The period is kept but not printed; add a **Service period** column to print it.

### Periods filled in from the contract

An invoice created from a contract fills in each line's period from the billing cycle of the service:

| **Cycle starts from** (in the service catalog) | Period filled in |
|---|---|
| **Period end** | The calendar period that ends on the billing date. A monthly service billed on 30 November 2026 gets `Nov 2026`. |
| **Signing date** | From the billing date to the day before the next billing date. A yearly service billed on 15 March 2026 gets `15 Mar 2026 – 14 Mar 2027`. |
| **Financial year end** or **Fixed date** | Nothing. Enter the period by hand if needed. |

A **One-time** service gets no period. When one line covers several billing dates, it gets the earliest start and the latest end; if any of them gives no period, the line gets none.

## Tax-inclusive amounts

By default, prices are entered without GST and GST is added on top. When the client has agreed a price that already includes GST, set **Amounts are** to **Tax inclusive** on the **Settings** tab. The choice is made for each invoice or credit note.

**Amounts are** is offered when the issuing entity is GST-registered. It is also shown on a document that is already tax inclusive, so that it can be switched back.

In **Tax inclusive** mode, the prices, line amounts and adjustments you enter include GST. Operon works the GST back from them: for each tax code, GST = amount × rate ÷ (100% + rate), rounded to the cent. The amount excluding GST is the amount less that GST. The total is the amount you entered.

For example, one SR line of 100.00 at 9%:

| | Amount (SGD) |
|---|---|
| **Subtotal (incl. GST)** | 100.00 |
| **Total excluding GST** | 91.74 |
| **GST 9% (included)** | 8.26 |
| **Total** | 100.00 |

GST is 100.00 × 9 ÷ 109 = 8.257…, rounded to 8.26, and 100.00 − 8.26 = 91.74. The invoice prints these lines in this order, with the note **Amounts are inclusive of GST.** under the table.

Duplicates and credit notes keep the mode of the invoice they come from.

## The customer reference

**Reference** on the **Association** tab holds the client's purchase order number or their own reference.

- When filled in, it is printed as **Reference** beside the dates on the invoice, the online copy and the PDF. When it is empty, nothing is printed.
- The invoice list search finds an invoice by its reference.
- It can still be changed after a payment or credit is recorded, because it is not an amount. A paid or void invoice cannot be changed at all, the reference included.
- A credit note created from an invoice takes the invoice's reference. A duplicate starts with no reference.

## The rest of the paper

- **Title**: select it to edit it.
- **Number**: shown as a placeholder until the invoice is issued.
- **Issue date**: set to the day of issue when the invoice is issued.
- **Due date**: choose a number of days from the issue date or **Custom date**.
- **Logo**: **Upload logo**, **Replace logo** or **Remove logo** (PNG, JPG or SVG).
- **To** and **From** rows: drag to reorder, **Delete row**, or **Add** a **Text** row or a **Field** row that is filled from the client or the issuing entity.
- **Add a description** and **Add a footnote** add free text.

{% aside type="caution" title="Edit after issue" %}
An issued invoice can still be edited while no payment and no credit is recorded on it. It keeps its number and its issuing entity, and its total must stay above zero. Once a payment or a credit is recorded, only the description, the footer note and the reference can be changed; the lines (with their tax codes and service periods), the adjustments and **Amounts are** are locked. A paid or void invoice cannot be edited.
{% /aside %}
